bbb: propagate_moves gave a loop exit the wrong value of the moved register.

opt_propagate_moves takes a loop with a register copy pair

    .L1:  move.l src,dst  ...  (exit: jcc .Lout)  ...  move.l dst,src  jcc .L1

and moves the first copy in front of the loop and the second behind it.
Inside the loop src is then no longer updated, so on every exit between the
two copies src must be set from dst again: src = dst + fixup, where fixup
undoes the auto increments of dst before the exit. Two bugs (issue #36):

1. For an auto increment in the source of an insn, the size was taken from
   the mode of the destination. After bbb pass 0 the byte load is
   "(set (strict_low_part (reg:QI d1)) (mem:QI (post_inc a0)))", and a
   strict_low_part is VOIDmode, so the increment counted as 0. Now the size
   of the memory read is used.

2. For two address registers and fixup 0 nothing was emitted at the exit,
   so src kept its value from before the loop. Now src = dst is emitted.

Reproducer (-O2 -m68020; the default -fbbb is needed, pass 0 included):

    long f(const unsigned char *s, unsigned char *d, unsigned char c,
           unsigned char m, const unsigned char *lim, int n, unsigned char *x0,
           unsigned char *x1, unsigned char *x2, unsigned char *x3)
    {
      const unsigned char *p = s; long acc = 0; int k = 0;
      while (k < n)
      {
        const unsigned char *q = p;
        if ((*q & m) != 0) goto out;
        acc += *q++;
        p = q; k++;
      }
    out:
      return (long)(p - s) * 3 + acc;
    }

Wrong code: the loop reads with "move.b (a0)+,d1" and leaves on "jne .L9";
.L9 computed p - s from a1, which still held s, so every early exit after
the first iteration returned acc instead of 3 * (p - s) + acc. Now .L9 uses
a0 - 1 (the p of the iteration that left the loop), the same as -fbbb=-.

--- a/gcc/bbb-opts.c
+++ b/gcc/bbb-opts.c
@@ -3297,7 +3297,7 @@
 						fixup += 0; // direct use
 					      else if (GET_CODE(x) == PRE_INC ||
 					      GET_CODE(x) == POST_INC)
-						fixup -= GET_MODE_SIZE(GET_MODE(dst));
+						fixup -= GET_MODE_SIZE(GET_MODE(src)); // size read: a strict_low_part dest is VOIDmode (issue #36)
 					      else if (GET_CODE(dst) == PRE_DEC ||
 					      GET_CODE(dst) == POST_DEC)
 						fixup += GET_MODE_SIZE(GET_MODE(dst));
@@ -3390,6 +3390,13 @@
 					      dstj, gen_rtx_PLUS (Pmode, dsti, gen_rtx_CONST_INT (Pmode, fixups[k])));
 					  emit_insn_before (neu, before);
 					}
+				      else if (REGNO(dsti) != REGNO(dstj))
+					{
+					  /* Two address registers and no offset: the exit still needs
+					   * src = dst, since src is no longer updated inside the loop
+					   * (issue #36). */
+					  emit_insn_before (gen_rtx_SET(dstj, dsti), before);
+					}
 				    }
 				}
 			      ++change_count;
